>> title: Butter Chicken
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: chicken, indian, tomato, butter, curry
>> counters: Curry House
>> aka: murgh makhani, murg makhani, makhani chicken, butter chicken masala, chicken makhani
>> pairs-with: makhani-gravy, chicken-tikka, naan, pilau-rice
>> servings: 6
>> time: 5 hr
>> slack: narrow — the black places on the chicken are the dish, and the twelve minutes under the broiler is the whole of them: past that the thigh dries out, short of it there is no char, and chicken poached in the sauce instead is a tomato-cashew stew and not this
>> step.1: marinate 4 hr, overnight if you can
>> step.2: broil 12 min, turning once, until the edges char
>> step.3: simmer 10 min
>> step.4: fold in off the heat

Marinate @boneless chicken thighs{2%lb}(900 g; cut in 2-in pieces) with @thick yogurt{1/2%cup}(120 g), @ginger-garlic paste{2%Tbs}(34 g), @Kashmiri chile powder{2%tsp}, @garam masala{1%tsp}, @lemon juice{1%Tbs}(15 mL) and @kosher salt{2%tsp} ~marinate{4%hr}, overnight if the day allows it.

Broil @&(~1)marinated chicken{} threaded on skewers under a #broiler{} on the top rung ~broil{12%min}, turning once, until the edges have gone black in places. Those black places are the dish. Chicken poached in the sauce instead is a tomato-cashew stew and not this.

Simmer @&(~1)charred chicken{} in @makhani gravy{5%cup}(1.2 L) ~simmer{10%min}, scraping the skewer tray into the pot with a splash of water.

Fold @cold butter{4%Tbs}(56 g; cubed), @heavy cream{1/4%cup}(60 mL) and @kasuri methi{2%tsp}(crumbled between the palms) into @&(~1)curry{} off the heat, a cube at a time.

The gravy already has butter whisked into it; this is the second lot, and it is the half the dish is named for. Chicken is the printed line, but the same gravy takes paneer for the vegetarian column, and the tikka on the skewer here is the same tikka that goes out on its own plate as a starter — this is a menu where one marinade prints twice.
